.TH WAVE-UNINSTALL 1 "" "LinuxWave" "LinuxWave Manual"

.SH NAME
wave-uninstall \- Uninstall one package version, several of them, or every version. Packages can be listed with commas or spaces, and one package can name several versions (ffmpeg@6.1@6.0). The unversioned link falls back to the highest remaining version, and goes away with the last one.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B wave uninstall <package>[@<version>|@all], ... [flags]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Uninstall one package version, several of them, or every version.
Packages can be listed with commas or spaces, and one package can name
several versions (ffmpeg@6.1@6.0). The unversioned link falls back to
the highest remaining version, and goes away with the last one.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-no\-link
Do not touch the unversioned link (the old name --unlink still works)
.TP
.B \-a, \-\-all
Uninstall every installed version of the package (the same as @all)

.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
wave uninstall jq
wave uninstall ffmpeg@6.1
wave uninstall ffmpeg@6.1@6.0
wave uninstall jq, yq
wave uninstall ffmpeg -a
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
wave(1)
